[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mCompute only[39m
     [38;5;246mValidator returns a result (valid + per-field errors); each form decides how to display. Smallest surface, easiest
[39m     [38;5;246mto test, no DOM dependency. Today's code just console.errors.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Compute + render errors
     [38;5;246mValidator also writes messages into the DOM next to each field. More reuse per form, but couples validation to [39m
     [38;5;246mmarkup conventions and needs error-element structure in index.html.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Compute + wire up submit
     [38;5;246mA helper takes a form element and rules, attaches the submit listener, reads values, validates, and calls your [39m
     [38;5;246mhandler. Most reuse, largest surface — it owns the whole form lifecycle.[39m
